==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|rot|rót|root|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*wrōts}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*wrd-||root}}; compare with English {{term|wort|lang=en}} and the Latin {{term/t|la|rādīx||root}}. Cognate with the Faroese {{term|rót|lang=fo}}; Old English {{term/t|ang|rōt}} (whence the Middle English word {{term|root||the underground part of a plant}} came, whence the English {{term|root|lang=en}} came).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/rouːt/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ouːt|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|rótar|rætur}}

# {{context|plant|lang=is}} [[root]]
# the [[roots]] of something, the [[beginning]] or [[origin]]
#: '''''Rætur''' fjallsins eru [[grasi vaxinn|grasi vaxnar]].''
#:: The '''foot''' of the mountain is covered with grass.
# {{context|mathematics|lang=is}} [[root]]
# {{context|linguistics|lang=is}} [[root]]
#: ''Hvernig finnur maður '''rót''' nafnorða?''
#:: How does one find the '''root''' of nouns?

